# Live and PACKS are one fabric

There is **one** routing file per region: R2 `dirt-packs/{id}/graph.v2.bin` + `geometry.v1.bin`.

- iOS PACKS downloads that object.
- Live `POST /api/route` loads **that same object**.
- Downloaded vs cellular is delivery, not a second road network.
- `longhaul.v1.json.gz` is a thinned highway extract. It is **not** Dirt. Do not point `/api/route` at it.

## When you change routing

| Change | Ship both |
| --- | --- |
| OSM / stitches / capillary / pack rebuild | Publish `graph.v2.bin` + `geometry.v1.bin` to R2 (that **is** live and download). Then `node scripts/pack-fabric/scripts/ship-routing.js --assert`. |
| Cost tables / Allow / search | Update `OnDeviceProfileCosts.swift` **and** `scripts/pack-fabric/routing/lib/profile-costs.js` **and** copy that JS into Mayday `routing/lib/profile-costs.js`, then deploy `/api/route`. Pack binaries unchanged. |
| Live graph loader (`select.js`, `graph.js`) | Commit + deploy Mayday from a **clean** tree. Never `vercel --prod` from `Documents/Mayday` when overlay chunks are dirty. |

A routing change that is only on the phone, or only on live, is **not shipped**.

## Do not

- Auto-download packs to “make live match.” Live must already be the pack.
- Deploy Mayday from a dirty overlay tree (uploads hundreds of MB, easy to miss the three routing files).
- Leave `useLonghaulPacks = onVercel` or `preferLonghaulPacks: true` on a path that chooses the graph file.
- Publish a second “live extract.”

## Commands

```
node scripts/pack-fabric/scripts/ship-routing.js --assert
node scripts/pack-fabric/scripts/ship-routing.js --pack bc
node scripts/pack-fabric/scripts/ship-routing.js --live
```

Mayday lives at `/Users/richardsmith/Documents/Mayday`. Production API: `https://dirt-mayday.vercel.app/api/route`.
